#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Lohia vs JP:* Rammanohar Lohia coined *"Non-Congressism"* (1967); Jayaprakash Narayan proclaimed *"Total Revolution"* (1974). Never confuse them!
  2. *Grounds of 1975 Emergency:* Declared under Article 352 on ground of *"internal disturbance"*. *"Armed rebellion"* was introduced by the 44th Amendment in 1978.
  3. *Allahabad Judge vs Vacation Judge:* *Justice Jagmohan Lal Sinha* invalidated Indira's election (12 June 1975); *Justice V.R. Krishna Iyer* granted conditional stay (24 June 1975).
  4. *Dissenter in ADM Jabalpur:* *Justice H.R. Khanna* was the sole dissenter defending personal liberty; *Justice A.N. Ray* was the CJI who authored the majority ruling.
  5. *42nd vs 44th Amendment:* 42nd (1976) *increased* Lok Sabha term to 6 years; 44th (1978) *restored* term to 5 years and made Articles 20 and 21 inviolable.
  6. *North vs South 1977 Pattern:* Congress was NOT routed everywhere; it was wiped out in North India (0 seats in UP/Bihar) but held its ground in South India (Andhra/Karnataka).
  7. *First Non-Congress PM:* *Morarji Desai* (March 1977), NOT Charan Singh or Atal Bihari Vajpayee.
]

